  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q53-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "53",
    "prompt": "In the expansion of $(1-x)^4\\left(1+\\dfrac1x\\right)^6$, find:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q53-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "The term independent of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$.\n\nMatch equal powers of $x$ and $x^{-1}$, then add the five contributions.",
          "worked": "Multiplying the general terms gives\n$$\\begin{align*}T_{k,r}&=\\binom4k(-x)^k\\binom6r x^{-r}\\\\T_{k,r}&=(-1)^k\\binom4k\\binom6r x^{k-r}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the constant term, $k-r=0$, so $(k,r)=(0,0),(1,1),(2,2),(3,3),(4,4)$. Let $C_0$ be the constant term.\n$$\\begin{align*}C_0&=\\sum_{k=0}^{4}(-1)^k\\binom4k\\binom6k\\\\C_0&=1-24+90-80+15\\\\C_0&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q53-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The coefficient of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-8$.\n\nUse $k-r=1$ and add the four matching coefficient products.",
          "worked": "Multiplying the general terms gives\n$$\\begin{align*}T_{k,r}&=\\binom4k(-x)^k\\binom6r x^{-r}\\\\T_{k,r}&=(-1)^k\\binom4k\\binom6r x^{k-r}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the term in $x$, $k-r=1$, so $(k,r)=(1,0),(2,1),(3,2),(4,3)$. Let $C_1$ be its coefficient.\n$$\\begin{align*}C_1&=\\sum_{k=1}^{4}(-1)^k\\binom4k\\binom6{k-1}\\\\C_1&=-4+36-60+20\\\\C_1&=-8.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
    ]
  },
